Track 3: Did the Estuary Boundary Drift?
- Story & Context: When morning arrived at the salt marshes of Bang Khun Thian, the surveyors found that the low-tide boundary markers had physically rearranged themselves to match the rhythmic delays of the Elders' dawn session. Salt-frost coated the aluminum horns of the sampan sound systems, leaving the patrol guards shivering as low-frequency sub-drops vibrated the silt beneath their boots until the dikes cracked. No bodies or boats remained in the gray sunrise, only the dying resonant hum of an open A-string and a spectral voice looping through the mangroves: "No surveyor stakes survive the black canal."
